For almost every question, try this structure:

Requirement

We need to handle 100k concurrent booking attempts.

Constraints

Correctness is critical, but throughput is also important.

Options

SQL optimistic locking vs Redis reservation layer.

Trade-off

SQL gives strong consistency but may bottleneck under extreme contention.

Decision

Redis reservation layer with atomic Lua scripts and durable persistence.

Failure Handling

TTL expiry, durable datastore as system of record, rebuild on recovery.

That structure makes an interviewer think, "This person can drive architecture discussions," which is exactly what Cleartrip will be evaluating in an Architect exploratory round.